Project: DayZero - Windows setup toolkit on a USB stick.
- builder\  : USB Builder (PowerShell 5.1 + WPF). Builder.ps1 + Builder.xaml. Writes autounattend.xml and copies kit\ to the stick.
- kit\      : runs on the new PC. DayZero.ps1 = wizard. kit\lib\*.psm1 = modules (order in Modules.ps1).
- kit\config\*.json : modes, apps (winget IDs), tweaks, debloat levels, drivers, office. Most changes are JSON only.
- kit\ui\Theme.xaml : all colours/styles (monochrome). Keep resource key names (DzMagenta etc.), code uses them.
- tests\    : Pester tests. Run: pwsh tools\Invoke-DzChecks.ps1 (tests + PSScriptAnalyzer). Must stay green.

Hard rules:
- .ps1/.psm1 files must be plain ASCII (PowerShell 5.1). .cmd files keep CRLF.
- autounattend.xml must never select, wipe or partition a disk.
- Never disable Windows Update or Defender; no third-party activators.
- Every tweak must be reversible (backup + DayZero.cmd -Undo); no scripts in JSON.
- winget IDs must be real (check winget-pkgs), never guessed.
- Don't use "$name?" inside strings (write "${name}?").

Workflow: small change -> run the checks -> fix -> commit.